":"Answer","text":"Some of the highest-paying roles include data scientist, machine learning engineer, AI engineer, data architect, and data engineering roles, especially in large companies and technology-driven industries.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-science-future\/#faq-question-1775734215502","position":6,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-science-future\/#faq-question-1775734215502","name":"6. How much can a data scientist earn in India?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Freshers in India can typically earn \u20b96\u201312 LPA, while experienced professionals often earn \u20b915\u201330+ LPA, depending on skills, city, company, and specialization in AI or ML.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-science-future\/#faq-question-1775734239736","position":7,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-science-future\/#faq-question-1775734239736","name":"7. Is coding necessary for a career in data science?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, coding is an important part of data science because languages like Python, SQL, and R are used for data analysis, machine learning models, and automation tasks.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-science-future\/#faq-question-1775734246946","position":8,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-science-future\/#faq-question-1775734246946","name":"8. What industries will need data scientists in the future?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Industries such as healthcare, finance, e-commerce, education, manufacturing, logistics, and IT will continue to require data scientists for analytics, forecasting, and AI-driven solutions.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":